<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Inkwell — Blogs</title>

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;600;700&family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,400;6..72,500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="shell">
      <!-- ========== top bar ========== -->
      <header class="topbar">
        <a class="brand" href="/">
          <span class="brand__mark">✒</span>
          <span class="brand__name">Inkwell</span>
        </a>

        <nav class="nav">
          <a class="nav__link" href="/">Home</a>
          <a class="nav__link nav__link--active" href="/blogs">Blogs</a>
          <a class="nav__link" href="/compose">Compose</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <!-- ========== page heading ========== -->
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="hero__kicker">Everything, newest first</p>

        <h1 class="hero__title">
          The
          <span>blog</span>
        </h1>

        <div class="hero__actions">
          <!-- TODO (student) — post count
               Print the real number of posts inside this chip,
               before the word "published". -->
          <span class="chip">
            <span class="chip__dot"></span>
            0 published
          </span>

          <a class="btn" href="/compose">New post</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section-head">
        <h2>All posts</h2>

        <!-- TODO (student) — same count again, formatted as "N total" -->
        <span class="section-head__count">0 total</span>
      </section>

      <!--
        TODO (student) — render every post

        1. Loop over the `posts` array that your route passes in, and repeat
           the <li class="post"> block below once per post.
        2. Grab the loop index too — you need it for .post__index (start at 1).
        3. Fill in the real values:
             .post__title  -> post title
             .post__meta   -> author inside <b>, then the created date
                              (a Date has .toDateString() if you want it short)
             .post__body   -> the full content of the post
        4. Delete both sample cards below once the loop works.

        Heads up: the content is user-typed text, so print it with the
        ESCAPING output tag, not the raw one. Ask yourself which of the two
        EJS output tags escapes HTML — that's the one you want here.
      -->
      <ul class="post-list">
        <li class="post">
          <div class="post__top">
            <span class="post__index">1</span>
            <h3 class="post__title">Sample post title goes here</h3>
          </div>

          <p class="post__meta">By <b>Author name</b> · Some date</p>

          <p class="post__body">
            These two cards exist only to show you the styling and the entrance
            animation (each card is staggered 60ms after the one above it).
            Replace them with your loop.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="post">
          <div class="post__top">
            <span class="post__index">2</span>
            <h3 class="post__title">A second sample post</h3>
          </div>

          <p class="post__meta">By <b>Someone else</b> · Some other date</p>

          <p class="post__body">
            Long posts wrap and breathe here. The stylesheet keeps line breaks
            you typed in the textarea, so paragraphs survive.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <!--
        TODO (student) — empty state

        Show the block below only when `posts` is empty, and hide the list
        above in that case.
      -->
      <div class="empty">
        <div class="empty__emoji">🗒️</div>
        <p>No posts yet</p>
        <a class="btn" href="/compose">Write your first post</a>
      </div>

      <p class="footnote">Built with Express · EJS · MongoDB</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
